European human rights law, particularly as articulated in the European Convention on Human Rights (ECHR), seeks to balance the right to freedom of assembly with considerations of public order, safety, and the rights of others through a framework that allows for certain restrictions on this right. Article 11 of the ECHR guarantees the right to peaceful assembly, but it also acknowledges that this right is not absolute. 

